{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Every man by his standard, with signs, by their fathers' houses.</b> We find in several midrashim (Numbers Rabbah 2:2–6) that greatly magnify the matter of the standards, and they expounded concerning them the verse ״וּבְשֵׁם אֱלֹהֵינוּ נִדְגֹּל״ (Psalms 20:6) — that at the time of the giving of the Torah, Israel saw the angels arrayed standard by standard, and they yearned to be standards like them. And concerning the verse (Song 6:10) ״מִי זֹאת הַנִּשְׁקָפָה כְּמוֹ שָׁחַר״, they expounded (Numbers Rabbah 2:4) that the nations would gaze at the excellence of Israel and were amazed, etc., and would say ״שׁוּבִי שׁוּבִי הַשּׁוּלַמִּית״ — cleave to us and come to us and we will make of you dukes and governors, and Israel would reply: ״מַה תֶּחֱזוּ בַּשּׁוּלַמִּית כִּמְחֹלַת הַמַּחֲנָיִם״ (Song 7:1) — that is to say, what greatness do you offer us? Can you possibly give us greatness such as our Elohim gave — the standard of the camp of Judah eastward, etc.? And every thoughtful person will wonder: what is this great tumult, and why does 'the city's voice roar' (I Kings 1:41) over this, and what preciousness and greatness was wrought in Israel that all the nations should so yearn for them?" "And what seems right to me to say on this matter is that the principal desire of Israel was to show all the peoples that the name of HaShem is called upon them, so that they would fear them, and through this they would raise the standard of exaltation and victory in all four directions of the world. For through their being surrounded in all four directions with the Shekhinah and the Ark in the middle — so that all face toward it — all the peoples would see that they go in the name of HaShem. And this is the sign toward which the eyes of all who dwell in the circle around it are directed, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Ta'anit 31a there): in the future the Holy One, blessed be He, will make a dance for the righteous in the Garden of Eden, and His glory, blessed be He, will be in the middle, as it says (Leviticus 26:12): ״וְהִתְהַלַּכְתִּי בְּתוֹכְכֶם״ — for every direction the righteous turn, it is all toward the face of the Shekhinah, and so too in this world. And this is the sign of the standard, for it is the sign of victory in war, and this standard is in the name of HaShem, for not by their sword did they inherit the land, but by the name of HaShem. And likewise the angels — because they surround the throne of His glory, blessed be He — their dread is upon all created beings, as it is written ״אֲיֻמָּה כַּנִּדְגָּלוֹת״ (Song 6:10). For through this surrounding, their dread will be upon all the nations like that of the angels, whom all fear. And concerning these standards Jacob was assured, as it says of him (Genesis 28:14): ״וּפָרַצְתָּ יָמָּה״ etc. Therefore it says ״אִישׁ עַל דִּגְלוֹ בְאֹתֹת״ — that is, with the signs that their father Jacob delivered to them, etc., for in a vision the matter of the standards was shown to him through the verse ״וּפָרַצְתָּ יָמָּה״ etc. Therefore the psalm begins (Psalms 20:2–6): ״יְשַׂגֶּבְךָ שֵׁם אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב״ etc., and concerning this it says ״וּבְשֵׁם אֱלֹהֵינוּ נִדְגֹּל״ — to raise the standard of exaltation and victory in all four directions in the name of our Elohim. Therefore they said ״מַה תֶּחֱזוּ בַּשּׁוּלַמִּית״ etc. — for your victory is human victory, and none of this compares to כִּמְחֹלַת הַמַּחֲנָיִם, which signifies divine victory. For ״הֵמָּה כָּרְעוּ וְנָפָלוּ״ — it is doubtful whether they are victorious, whereas ״וַאֲנַחְנוּ קַּמְנוּ וַנִּתְעוֹדָד״ — for surely all who fight in the name of HaShem are victorious. And furthermore, the essence is lacking among you, namely the appearance of the glory of HaShem — that is the sign toward which all who dwell around the center direct themselves. Therefore it says ״בְאֹתֹת״, in order that the Shekhinah be for them a sign toward which their eyelids are directed."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:39:43.036567833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}